[0.000, "o", "Equal(10);\\n  });\\n});\",\"description\":\"Test that verifies pagination controls work correctly including page size changes and navigation buttons\"}],\"testContext\":\"The photo gallery displays photos in a grid layout with filtering and pagination. The main selectors are: .photo-grid for the container, .photo-card for individual cards, #year-select for year filtering, and standard pagination controls. Images have a data-fallback attribute for placeholder handling. The test database contains 14 photos across years 2008, 2014, and 2026. CRITICAL: The year select options have trailing whitespace in their text content (e.g., '2008\\\\n        '), so selection must be done using the value attribute rather than text content. Year filtering works by selecting from a dropdown and clicking Apply Filters, which can be reset with Clear Filters. Pagination supports page sizes of 10, 25, 50, 100, and 250, with navigation via First, Prev, Next, and Last links.\",\"explanation\":\"The test failure was caused by whitespace in the HTML "]
[0.000, "o", "template for year options. The template has newlines and spaces after the year text: '<option value=\\\"2008\\\">2008\\\\n        </option>'. When using .allTextContents(), this returns '2008\\\\n        ' instead of '2008', causing selectOption() to fail to find a matching option. The fix is to iterate through options and extract the value attribute directly, then use selectOption({ value: selectedYear }) instead of selectOption(selectedYear). This bypasses the text matching issue entirely and uses the clean value attribute.\",\"confidence\":0.98}\r\n"]
